==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|gostly}}, {{m|enm|gastlich}}, from {{inh|en|ang|gāstlīċ|t=spiritual, holy, clerical (not lay), ghastly, ghostly, spectral}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*gaistalīk|t=spiritual}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|ghost|ly|id2=adjectival}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|ghaistly}}, {{m|sco|gaistly|t=spiritual, ghastly, terrifying}}, {{cog|fy|geastlik|t=spiritual, clerical, religious}}, {{cog|nl|geestelijk|t=spiritual, clerical, ecclesiastical}}, {{cog|de|geistlich|t=spiritual, sacred, religious}}, {{cog|da|geistlig|t=ecclesiastical, clerical}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɡoʊstli/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-ghostly.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|oʊstli|q1=General American|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# Of or pertaining to [[ghost]]s or [[spirit]]s.
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:ghostly}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''ghostly''' figure with a hood}}
#: {{ux|en|The graveyard was haunted by a '''ghostly''' figure of a young girl.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''ghostly''' moaning was heard from upstairs.}}
# [[spooky|Spooky]]; [[frightening]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:frightening}}
#: {{ux|en|A '''ghostly''' hush fell.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1929|author=Robert Dean Frisbee|title=The Book of Puka-Puka|publisher=Eland|year_published=2019|page=35
|passage=Scores of coconut-shell fires blazed with their characteristic glaring white flame, throwing grotesque shadows on the brown thatched huts, dancing in fairylike shimmerings among the domes of coconut fronds, casting '''ghostly''' reaches of light through the adjacent graveyards, and silhouetting the forms of ''pareu''-clad natives at work cleaning their fish or laying them on the live coals to broil.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=Dave Eggers|title=The Parade|publisher=Vintage Books|location=N.Y.|page=134
|passage=His lips were chapped and lined with a '''ghostly''' purple fringe.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} Relating to the [[soul]]; not [[carnal]] or [[secular]]; [[spiritual]].
#: ''a '''ghostly''' confessor''
#* {{RQ:Book of Common Prayer
|passage=Save and defend us from our '''ghostly''' enemies.}}
#* {{RQ:Taylor Holy Living|passage=one of the '''ghostly''' children of St. Jerome}}

